# Contexer Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env in a project, or skip it: `contexer setup` saves a
# provider, your key and models for every project in ~/.contexer/ (14
# providers; `contexer models --providers` lists them). Variables here and in
# your environment take precedence over what setup saved.
#
# A model is needed only to DRAFT checks from a goal (`contract draft`,
# `verify "<goal>"`, `run "<goal>"`) and for the coding agent. Replaying
# approved contracts never calls a model. With several keys set, Contexer
# drafts with Anthropic, then OpenAI, then OpenRouter, unless
# CONTEXER_LLM_PROVIDER or [compiler] in contexer.toml says otherwise. Draft
# quality depends heavily on the model: see bench/RESULTS.md.

# Anthropic (https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# OpenAI, or any OpenAI-compatible gateway via OPENAI_BASE_URL
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Force a provider for drafting: any id from `contexer models --providers`
# CONTEXER_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# OpenRouter API Key (also used by the interactive shell's chat agent)
# Obtain from https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here

# OpenRouter's free models allow 50 requests a day (1,000 after buying $10 of
# credit); a small change took about 15. `contexer doctor` shows what is left.
#
# OpenRouter model for drafting checks. Leave unset for the default,
# nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free (measured: 33/40 seeded bugs caught),
# which falls back to openrouter/free when unavailable. openrouter/free alone
# picks a different free model per request and gives inconsistent drafts.
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

# Optional OpenRouter attribution headers
OPENROUTER_SITE_URL=https://github.com/murtuza777/contexer-agent
OPENROUTER_APP_NAME=Contexer

# Logging & Output
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
VERBOSE=false

# GitHub for `contexer run --pr`, `--issue` and commit statuses: GITHUB_TOKEN,
# or nothing at all if you are logged in with `gh auth login`.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here

# GitHub for the interactive shell's GitHub MCP server
# Create a Personal Access Token with repo (read) scope at https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_github_pat_here
# Optional: toolsets (defaults to repos,issues)
# GITHUB_TOOLSETS=repos,issues
# Optional: force read-only (defaults to true)
# GITHUB_READ_ONLY=true

